                        "form": "коле́чке"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b316de8e-0b1d-42b8-9d0f-a15ab3cd98ae",
                        "entry_id": "b3c46507-e52c-30fc-8d85-d7c1448c617d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "коле́чках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f56d7b3-da6f-3551-9995-6964f27faf8a",
                        "entry_id": "b3c46507-e52c-30fc-8d85-d7c1448c617d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "уменьш. к кольцо; небольшое кольцо (форма или предмет такой формы)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "80d56add-fc8a-4842-b616-8e279bc0b248",
                                "sense_id": "3f56d7b3-da6f-3551-9995-6964f27faf8a",
                                "text": "Он был среднего роста, худощав, недурен лицом, черноволос и немного кудряв; молодые усы завивались у него в тоненькие колечки."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3de11ae-705e-4969-922f-dc7ece1d68f5",
                                "sense_id": "3f56d7b3-da6f-3551-9995-6964f27faf8a",
                                "text": "— Попробуй как-нибудь, — говорит ротный, задумчиво выпустив изо рта колечко табачного дыма."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06e1d9be-aeee-469c-9b43-b007dc5ab310",
                                "sense_id": "3f56d7b3-da6f-3551-9995-6964f27faf8a",
                                "text": "Он остановился у прилавка, где, при красивом освещении, лежали маленькие золотые колечки."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f0865d6-9320-3259-9f85-48f530fa95bd",
                        "entry_id": "b3c46507-e52c-30fc-8d85-d7c1448c617d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "игра, в которой водящего выбирают при помощи кольца"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b727e392-499b-46d8-8df3-0d9eb8745a29",
                                "sense_id": "3f0865d6-9320-3259-9f85-48f530fa95bd",
                                "text": "Играли ли в колечко, в верёвочку или рублик, разговаривали ли, как теперь, Николай не отходил от Сони и совсем новыми глазами смотрел на неё."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee7d881a-c129-4c9d-986b-21eb2f0bfb68",
                        "source_entry_id": "b3c46507-e52c-30fc-8d85-d7c1448c617d",
                        "source_sense_description": "небольшое кольцо",
                        "target_lang_word": "ringlet",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ringlet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "afc48597-57bc-316d-b3cb-3dcc136b9012",
                                        "entry_id": "ac0a2a70-5aba-3617-9496-693428685e00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A small ring."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb0f2cc3-db17-3c16-880a-a8e7f2fedb90",
                                        "entry_id": "ac0a2a70-5aba-3617-9496-693428685e00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lock, tress."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12985f43-72b3-4e01-a26f-edba0a498e4e",
                                                "sense_id": "bb0f2cc3-db17-3c16-880a-a8e7f2fedb90",
                                                "text": "Her hair was in ringlets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c6289bc-c4e3-4b5d-891c-ac222ecbf817",
                                                "sense_id": "bb0f2cc3-db17-3c16-880a-a8e7f2fedb90",
                                                "text": "For knovv by lot from Jove I am the povvr / Of this fair VVood, and live in Oak'n bovvr, / To nurſe the Saplings tall, and curl the grove / VVith ringlets quaint, and vvanton vvindings vvove."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c30a1c9-b4d6-44b5-a4c1-80c9e87090a8",
                                                "sense_id": "bb0f2cc3-db17-3c16-880a-a8e7f2fedb90",
                                                "text": "She was both beautiful and young to their eyes. Her hair was a rich red in color and fell in flowing ringlets over her shoulders. Her dress was pure white but her eyes were blue, and they looked kindly upon the little girl."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7ceb84cc-7568-3426-8122-35a021384421",
                                        "entry_id": "ac0a2a70-5aba-3617-9496-693428685e00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various butterflies with small rings on the wings, in the tribe Satyrini of the family Nymphalidae, such as Aphantopus hyperantus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "ringlet",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e93c457c-7c31-3c59-af61-72004283e4d3",
                                        "entry_id": "45f366af-60a7-3dd1-ab37-b730ccdd310e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To form into ringlets."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ab0c247-c024-47a3-8e75-4b9c3f8c4d96",
                                                "sense_id": "e93c457c-7c31-3c59-af61-72004283e4d3",
                                                "text": "\"It's very becoming!\" said Pollie coaxingly, taking his curly head, which she had been brushing and ringleting for the last half hour, all damp, into her arms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abf76e01-71d7-3d5e-a5a8-e197aafa5052",
                                        "entry_id": "45f366af-60a7-3dd1-ab37-b730ccdd310e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To surround or encircle like a ringlet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa09cf0c-1be2-4708-a448-6b57769d3168",
                                                "sense_id": "abf76e01-71d7-3d5e-a5a8-e197aafa5052",
                                                "text": "I think now that if it had gripped me with those suckers, I would have gone out into the mist too. But it didn't. It grabbed Norm. And the third tentacle ringleted his other ankle. Now he was being pulled away from me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
